## 2. JSON Schemas

### 2.1 The Delegated Session Token (Internal)

Generated by the Local App when the user approves a **delegated** plan/budget (after the agent proposes). Used by the local deterministic engine for policy enforcement.

**MVP:** Only x402 payments; no other methods.

```json
{
  "session_id": "sess_8f92a1b",
  "agent_id": "agent_news_researcher_04",
  "issued_at": 1708230000,
  "expires_at": 1708316400,
  "policy": {
    "global_limit_atomic": 10000000,
    "per_tx_limit_atomic": 2000000,
    "allowed_methods": ["x402_pay"],
    "allowed_domains": ["*.weather.com", "api.newsapi.org"],
    "auto_approve": true
  },
  "signature": "local_device_signature"
}
```

### 2.2 Custom Skills (Agent-Facing) — Two Skills Required

The delegated flow requires **two** skills: the agent must **initiate authorization** (propose plan + budget) *before* it can pay at any x402. One skill alone cannot do both.

---

#### Skill 1: Request delegation (initiate user approval)

Call this **before** accessing any paywalled resource. Agent has decided a payment plan for the task and needs the user to approve it. This triggers the Local Portal to show the proposal and run Step-Up Auth; on approval, a delegated session is created.

```yaml
name: portal_request_delegation
description: Propose a budget and plan for a task that may require x402 payments. Call this BEFORE visiting any paywalled service. Triggers user approval on the Local Portal (Step-Up Auth). If approved, you get a delegated session and may later call portal_pay when you hit an HTTP 402. If denied, do not attempt paid access.
parameters:
  type: object
  properties:
    plan_summary:
      type: string
      description: Short description of what the agent will do and why it may need to pay (e.g., "Access 2 premium news APIs for research").
    budget_max:
      type: string
      description: Maximum amount to spend for this task (e.g., "5.00").
    currency:
      type: string
      enum: ["USDC"]
      default: "USDC"
  required: ["plan_summary", "budget_max"]
```

---

#### Skill 2: Pay at x402 (within approved session)

Call this **only after** the user has approved via Skill 1 and you have received "approved". Use when you actually get an HTTP 402 and need to pay within the pre-approved budget.

```yaml
name: portal_payment_proxy
description: Pay an x402 paywall within your pre-approved delegated budget. Only call after portal_request_delegation was approved and you hit an HTTP 402. Do NOT use for checking balances.
parameters:
  type: object
  properties:
    operation:
      type: string
      enum: ["x402_pay"]
      description: MVP supports only x402 paywall payments.
    amount:
      type: string
      description: The amount to send (e.g., "1.50").
    currency:
      type: string
      enum: ["USDC"]
      default: "USDC"
    recipient:
      type: string
      description: The x402 paywall URL or payment destination from the 402 response.
  required: ["operation", "amount", "recipient"]
```

